From 6020f763137d33b4d497f9b9d196150b2cfd815b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Etaash Mathamsetty <45927311+Etaash-mathamsetty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 23:06:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Avoid deadlocks with update_client_surfaces

Calling update_client_surfaces() from the fractional-scale listener is unsafe:
the listener runs on the Wayland event thread while holding win_data_mutex,
and the update can synchronously wait on a window thread which needs the same
mutex.  Besides deadlocking the two threads, this prevents the event thread
from delivering the initial xdg_surface configure after a fullscreen role
rebuild.

The regular window-position and expose paths update the client surfaces after
the scale change, so do not perform the update from the listener.

This restores 6020f763137d33b4d497f9b9d196150b2cfd815b from Etaash
Mathamsetty's wine-wayland series.  It was dropped during the latest rebase
while the unsafe call remained in the resulting source.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
index 782628581c6..fed890ec90b 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -1238,9 +1238,6 @@ void wp_fractional_scale_handle_scale(void* user_data,
 
     surface->window.scale = scale;
 
-    /* reattach client surfaces as their rects have changed */
-    update_client_surfaces(hwnd);
-
     wayland_win_data_release(data);
 
     request_window_surface_expose(hwnd, FALSE);
-- 
2.51.0

